    Show the model the plate when a file opens, and say what intent_update leaves unchecked

    The first message after a file opens now carries a picture of the active
    plate, the same offscreen iso render view_render gives, as the last part of
    the turn's message, when the plate has a printable object. It is rendered
    when the request is built and never stored or replayed. The same request
    ends with a developer item, built from the state at that moment: nothing is
    recorded about what the print is for, the picture is the plate as loaded,
    and the filament and process presets are to be checked once the purpose is
    known. The item is left out when a purpose is already recorded.

    intent_update's result ends with an unchecked sentence naming the printer,
    filament and process presets and the active plate's type in force as not yet
    checked against the purpose just recorded; the output schema requires it.

    view_render's description also offers the picture for telling what an object
    is. fileReportInstructions.ts gains one sentence about the picture and loses
    two it no longer needs. The Preparing section's inspect clause goes, since
    the result and the picture now prompt it where it applies: the prompt is
    2,717 bytes, from 2,741.

